KZ3 patch 1135 (SPU pass 112; diagnostic, off by default): KZ3_CPU_PROBE=1 (needs KZ3_WAIT_ACCT) samples the logical processor of every
thread that runs SPU code (every 256th spu_ib_direct hop, MFC tag-status read and MFC command). Each [wacct] thread line then
carries cpums= (the thread's CPU ms in the window), tid= and cpus=N:count,...; [cpu-topo] lines at start list each core's
logical processors, SMT flag and efficiency class (under Proton: 1 = P-core, 0 = E-core).

